            "keyPoints": [
                "Claude Fable 5.1 shipped September 1, 2026; the leaked file is named Claude-Fable-5.1.md in Pliny's CL4R1T4S repo.",
                "It is an extraction, not a hack — no Anthropic system was compromised.",
                "The '270,000 characters + private user memories' headline is contested: a direct read of the file reported ~180,000 characters and found no evidence of real memory data exposure.",
                "Anthropic itself publishes official (but narrower) system prompts in its release notes, so much of this material is already public.",
                "Most of the prompt is capability, not personality: tool schemas plus search and citation rules dominate; safety/behavior text is the smallest major block.",
                "It describes the consumer claude.ai surface — API calls carry no default system prompt, and Claude Code ships its own instructions.",
                "Fable 5.1 and Mythos 5.1 share the same weights; only the safeguard configuration and access differ."
            ],
