    "transcript": {
        "duration": 55.439998626708984,
        "text": "CloudFable 5.1 full system prompt leaked within an hour of its launch. Andropic's newest model got its system prompt leaked about one hour after it shipped on September 1st. Jailbreak researcher Blini published it as CloudFable 5.1.md in the public clarity repo on GitHub. So you can read it right now. The core prompt runs around 180,000 characters and roughly 20,007 words, and some versions floating around in an extra repo contain it 275,000 characters. That's up about 120 characters from the Fable 5 leak back in June. Inside, you get the exact two schemas, search and citation rules, safety classifier behavior, and the detailed rules for all Cloud's memory features files and the place where it learns about you. One thing to be clear on, this isn't a breach of the weight, servers, or user data. It's just an extraction of the instructions the model sees at runtime. If you want a link, just comment prompt and I'll send it to you.",
        "language": "english",
